@startuml openclaw-web-tools-flow
' ============================================================================
'  OpenClaw — DEEP DIVE: web research / browsing tools + how the agent
'  reasons its way to an answer.
'  Worked trace: "best steak places 1-3k yen near Kichijoji, open 7pm tomorrow"
'  Render:  java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng openclaw-web-tools-flow.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5A5A5A
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #999999
  FontStyle bold
  FontSize 13
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #888888
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #C9B458
}

title OpenClaw — Web Tools Deep Dive\nHow web_search / web_fetch / browser feed the LLM, and how the agent decides its way to the final answer\nTrace: "best steak places within 1-3k yen near Kichijoji, open from 7pm tomorrow"

' ===========================================================================
' THE LOOP CORE (condensed — full version in openclaw-flow.puml)
' ===========================================================================
package "CORE AGENT LOOP  ·  src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt.ts" #EDE7F6 {
  rectangle "**① LLM turn**\nsystem prompt (tool descriptions tell the model:\n'web_search = current info', 'web_fetch = read a page')\n+ full transcript + user question\n→ model emits a **tool_call** or final text" as LLM #D8CCF0
  rectangle "**② Has tool_call?**\n<diamond>\nyes → run tool, append result, loop\nno  → text is the FINAL ANSWER" as DECIDE #C9B6F0
  rectangle "**③ append tool_result**\nto messages[] → back to ①\n(model now 'sees' the search/page content)" as APPEND #D8CCF0
}

note right of DECIDE
  **This is the agency.** Nothing hardcodes
  "search then fetch then answer". The model,
  each turn, looks at what it has and decides
  the next tool call. Typical research shape:
    search → (read snippets) → fetch a few
    pages → (maybe search again) → synthesize.
end note

' ===========================================================================
' TOOL A — web_search
' ===========================================================================
package "TOOL A · web_search   src/agents/tools/web-search.ts → src/web-search/runtime.ts" #E8F5E9 {

  rectangle "**createWebSearchTool.execute(args)**\nargs schema: query (req), count, country,\nlanguage, freshness(day/week/month/year),\ndate_after/before, domain_filter…\n<i>web-search.ts</i>" as WS_ENTRY #CDEBD0

  rectangle "**resolveWebSearchToolRuntimeContext()**\nlate-bind runtime creds/config so a long-lived\nagent picks up keys without rebuilding the tool" as WS_CTX #CDEBD0

  package "runWebSearch()  ·  provider resolution" #F1FBF2 {
    rectangle "**resolveWebSearchCandidates()**\norder providers by preference:\n1. explicit args.providerId\n2. runtime-selected provider\n3. config `tools.web.search.provider`\n4. auto-detect" as WS_CAND #DCF3DE
    rectangle "**resolveWebSearchProviderId()** — auto-detect\nfor each provider in priority order:\n• keyless? remember as last-resort fallback\n• requires key? use it IFF credential present\n  (env var / auth profile / config)\nelse fall back to first keyless provider" as WS_AUTO #DCF3DE
    rectangle "**hasExplicitWebSearchSelection?**\nyes → no fallback (fail hard on that provider)\nno  → allow fallback down the candidate list" as WS_FB #DCF3DE
  }

  rectangle "**candidate.createTool().execute(args)**\ncall the actual provider (Brave / Perplexity /\nGoogle / Bing / keyless) over HTTPS.\nLoop to next candidate on failure / missing-key\nstructured error (only when fallback allowed)" as WS_CALL #CDEBD0

  rectangle "**SEARCH_CACHE**\nnormalized-key cache of results\n(dedupes repeat queries in a run)" as WS_CACHE #FFE0B2

  rectangle "**jsonResult( results, provider )**\nnormalized list → [{title, url, snippet/age}]\nThis goes back into messages[] for the model" as WS_OUT #CDEBD0
}

' ===========================================================================
' TOOL B — web_fetch
' ===========================================================================
package "TOOL B · web_fetch   src/agents/tools/web-fetch.ts → src/web-fetch/runtime.ts" #E3F2FD {

  rectangle "**execute({url, extractMode, maxChars})**\nextractMode: markdown(default)|text\nmaxChars default 20k, response cap 750KB" as WF_ENTRY #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**sanitizeWebFetchUrl()**\nrepairs LLM-injected whitespace\n('https:// site' → 'https://site'),\nrequires http/https scheme" as WF_SAN #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**FETCH_CACHE check**\nkey = url+mode+maxChars+policy flags\nhit → return cached {…, cached:true}" as WF_CACHE #FFE0B2

  package "fetchWithWebToolsNetworkGuard()  ·  SSRF + transport" #EEF6FE {
    rectangle "**SSRF guard**  <i>src/infra/net/ssrf.js</i>\nresolve DNS, BLOCK private/loopback/link-local\n/metadata IPs (169.254.169.254 etc).\nSsrFBlockedError = hard stop (no fallback)" as WF_SSRF #DCEBFB
    rectangle "**HTTP GET**\nbrowser-like UA, Accept md/html,\nmaxRedirects=3, timeout, AbortSignal\nbody streamed, truncated at 750KB" as WF_HTTP #DCEBFB
  }

  rectangle "**Content-type branch**\n• text/markdown → use as-is (Cloudflare md)\n• text/html → Readability extraction\n• other → raw" as WF_BRANCH #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**extractReadableContent()**\n<i>web-fetch/content-extractors.runtime.ts</i>\nrun plugin extractors (Mozilla Readability)\nstrip nav/ads/boilerplate → main article\n→ htmlToMarkdown / markdownToText\nfallbacks: basic-html → raw" as WF_READ #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**truncateText(maxChars)**\nbound the payload; set truncated flag" as WF_TRUNC #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**wrapExternalContent() — UNTRUSTED**\nexternalContent:{untrusted:true, source:'web_fetch'}\nfences page text as data, NOT instructions\n(prompt-injection defense)" as WF_WRAP #FFCDD2

  rectangle "**provider fallback**\nif direct fetch fails / blocked-by-bot /\nReadability empty → try configured fetch\nprovider (e.g. Jina/Firecrawl) instead" as WF_PROV #CFE6FB

  rectangle "**jsonResult**\n{url, finalUrl, status, title, text(markdown),\nextractor, truncated, length, fetchedAt}\n→ back into messages[]" as WF_OUT #CFE6FB
}

' ===========================================================================
' TOOL C — browser (alternate branch: logged-in / interactive sites)
' ===========================================================================
package "TOOL C · browser (used instead of fetch for JS/login/forms)\nextensions/browser/src/browser-tool.ts" #FFF3E0 {
  rectangle "**navigate / open**\nChrome via CDP — target host|sandbox|node" as BR_NAV #FFE6C7
  rectangle "**snapshot (ARIA tree as text)**\nstable element `ref`s = how LLM 'sees' a page;\nwrapped UNTRUSTED. screenshot for vision." as BR_SNAP #FFE6C7
  rectangle "**act(kind)**: click/type/fill/select/press/\nhover/drag/wait/evaluate + upload/dialog\ntargets a `ref` from the last snapshot" as BR_ACT #FFE6C7
  rectangle "loop: snapshot → reason → act → snapshot\nuntil the goal state is reached" as BR_LOOP #FFE6C7
}

note bottom of BR_LOOP
  Reservations / LinkedIn / form-filling take THIS branch
  (real session cookies, dynamic JS, clicking).
  The steak query does NOT — static info pages = web_search + web_fetch.
end note

' ===========================================================================
' SECURITY RAILS (cross-cutting)
' ===========================================================================
package "SECURITY RAILS (apply to every web tool)" #FCE4EC {
  rectangle "**Credential resolution**\nenv var → auth profile → config;\nkeyless providers only as last resort" as SEC_CRED #F8BBD0
  rectangle "**SSRF policy**\nblocks internal/metadata IPs before any\nbyte is fetched" as SEC_SSRF #F8BBD0
  rectangle "**Untrusted-content wrapping**\nall fetched/scraped text fenced as data;\nmodel told not to obey instructions in it" as SEC_WRAP #F8BBD0
}

' ===========================================================================
' FINAL ANSWER node (declared before use)
' ===========================================================================
rectangle "**FINAL ANSWER (synthesis)**\nModel has accumulated: search hits + fetched\npage texts (hours, prices, addresses). It now\nreasons over them — filters by budget(1-3k¥),\nopen@19:00 Sat, near Kichijoji — ranks, and\nwrites prose. Streamed to terminal + saved\nto session JSONL." as FINAL #C8E6C9

' ===========================================================================
' EDGES — the loop
' ===========================================================================
LLM --> DECIDE
DECIDE --> APPEND : tool_call
APPEND --> LLM : loop

' web_search path
DECIDE --> WS_ENTRY : web_search(query, freshness…)
WS_ENTRY --> WS_CTX
WS_CTX --> WS_CAND
WS_CAND --> WS_AUTO
WS_AUTO --> WS_FB
WS_FB --> WS_CALL
WS_CALL --> WS_CACHE
WS_CACHE --> WS_OUT
WS_OUT --> APPEND : results[] back to model

' web_fetch path
DECIDE --> WF_ENTRY : web_fetch(url)
WF_ENTRY --> WF_SAN
WF_SAN --> WF_CACHE
WF_CACHE --> WF_SSRF : miss
WF_SSRF --> WF_HTTP
WF_HTTP --> WF_BRANCH
WF_BRANCH --> WF_READ : html
WF_READ --> WF_TRUNC
WF_BRANCH --> WF_TRUNC : md/raw
WF_TRUNC --> WF_WRAP
WF_WRAP --> WF_OUT
WF_HTTP ..> WF_PROV : fail/blocked
WF_READ ..> WF_PROV : empty
WF_PROV --> WF_WRAP
WF_OUT --> APPEND : page text back to model

' browser path
DECIDE --> BR_NAV : browser(navigate)
BR_NAV --> BR_SNAP
BR_SNAP --> BR_ACT
BR_ACT --> BR_LOOP
BR_LOOP --> APPEND : observed state back to model

' security wiring
WS_CALL ..> SEC_CRED
WF_SSRF ..> SEC_SSRF
WF_WRAP ..> SEC_WRAP
BR_SNAP ..> SEC_WRAP

' final
DECIDE --> FINAL : no tool_call

' ===========================================================================
' WORKED TRACE — the steak query, turn by turn
' ===========================================================================
note as TRACE #E3F2FD
  **WORKED TRACE — how the steak answer was actually built**
  ----
  **Turn 1** model: nothing yet → call
    web_search{ query:"steak restaurant Kichijoji", freshness/recency }
    → provider auto-detected by available key → results[]:
      Tabelog/Tablecheck pages, "Steak House Satou", "Yappari Steak", …
  **Turn 2** model sees hits, needs hours+price → 1..N parallel/serial
    web_fetch{ url: tabelog Satou } → SSRF ok → HTML → Readability →
    markdown: "営業時間 17:00–20:00 … ステーキ御膳 3,000円" (untrusted-wrapped)
  **Turn 3** web_fetch other candidates (Yappari, Center Beef, Rooftop Butcher)
    → hours, ¥ ranges, exit/location extracted the same way
  **Turn 4** (optional) web_search again to confirm "tomorrow = Saturday"
    hours or a place's current status
  **Turn 5** model has enough → NO tool_call → writes the ranked list:
    • filters to 1,000–3,000¥  • checks open at 19:00 Sat
    • adds vibe/location/last-order  • picks Top Pick
  ----
  Accuracy/freshness comes from the FETCHED PAGES, not model memory;
  the model's job is selection + filtering + synthesis over that evidence.
  (Caveat: if a page is stale or blocked, the answer inherits that — hours
   like "L.O. 20:00" are only as right as the source it read.)
end note
TRACE .. FINAL

legend left
  | Stage | What decides the next step |
  | LLM turn | model picks tool + args from the question + what it already has |
  | web_search | find candidate URLs + snippets (provider auto-resolved by key) |
  | web_fetch | turn ONE url into clean markdown (SSRF-guarded, Readability) |
  | browser | only when login/JS/forms needed (snapshot+act loop) |
  | synthesis | filter by constraints, rank, write — when no tool_call remains |
endlegend

@enduml
